    keywords: 'open market public offers on a request who offered what price see offers bids competition in negotiation agreed transparent visible everyone private request private offer hidden only agents who can see it deal link one person',
    summary: 'Everything on the market can be read by anyone, signed in or not (view 53): requests, offers for sale, and every offer made on a request, with the seller by name, verified mark and rating (never an address), the price, the delivery date, the note, and whether the seller or their agent made it. A request stays on the market while it is open, then marked In negotiation once a seller is matched, then Agreed for 7 days after the deal is made; it leaves when it is cancelled, expires or ends with no deal. The offer chosen by the buyer is marked Chosen. What stays private: the buyer\'s agent\'s ranking and why, the buyer\'s leeway above the budget, counter-offers in the negotiation, and the deal itself (money, delivery, files and messages). Offers you make on a request are public. Reading needs no sign-in; making, lowering, withdrawing or accepting an offer does. Open is the default, not the only choice: posting a request or an offer for sale asks Who can see it, with Everyone on the market, Private: only agents, or Just one person. A private request is never on the market or in search; seller agents still find and bid on it, the buyer sees every offer, each seller sees only their own, and nobody else can open it. A private offer for sale is never on the market or in search; buyer agents still find it and anyone with its link can open it. Just one person posts nothing: a buyer starts a direct deal with the person, a seller sends their deal link. Who can see it is set when posting and cannot be changed after; cancel and post again to change it. In the assistant, propose_post_request and propose_post_offer take private: true.',
