    tools: ['propose_post_offer', 'propose_take_down', 'get_my_market_activity', 'get_my_skills', 'set_way_i_deal', 'list_requests_that_fit_me', 'list_learned_suggestions', 'propose_learned_change', 'dismiss_learned_suggestion', 'propose_edit_offer', 'propose_stop_agent_bid'],
    keywords: 'get customers find clients sell offer listing advertise service seller agent bid supply grow business more buyers photo photos picture image report',
    summary: "Customers find you through your offers and your seller agent. An offer is a public listing with a title, description and asking price in USDC, and up to four photos. Photos are added on the offer form, or sent to the assistant: on the website pick, paste or drag the photo into the assistant box, where it waits with a remove button, and send it with words such as \"selling this\" (a photo sent with no words asks whether it is for an offer or an invoice); in Telegram or WhatsApp say in the caption that it is for your offer. The offer card the assistant shows adds the photos sent in the last hour. The first photo shows on the market card. Anyone signed in can report an offer or its photos from the offer page; the team reviews reports and can remove the photos. Your seller agent also reads new requests and makes offers for you when the work matches your skills; you approve the deal it brings. Two setup answers change this: with \"Ask me first\" the agent does not make offers, it asks you about each request that fits with the price it would offer (in the bell, the assistant, by email and on Telegram) and you answer with one tap or change the price; with \"I have clients\" only, your agent stays off the market and does not read new requests. Change either with set_up_my_agents or at /setup. A live offer's title, description and price can be changed, from /seller or by asking the assistant (propose_edit_offer), until it matches into a deal. A seller can also tell their agent to stop negotiating on one request (propose_stop_agent_bid) and make their own offer there instead. Each person also has the ways they deal, for selling and for buying, one per kind of deal: one-time, milestones (paid in stages), goods with delivery (review starts on arrival) and refundable deposit; the other kinds of the escrow family are added as they go live. Each way keeps the lowest price they take, their usual price and its time; there is no highest, a bigger budget gets an offer opened from the usual price (view 41). Only a usual price the person gave counts (in setup, on the Edit profile form, in the way editor or with set_way_i_deal); until then the agent opens from the budget of the request, never under their lowest. A usual price carried over from an old price range is shown but does not set the opening. Profile, Your agent (/profile/setup) sets the agent up on one page (view 45): whether it is on and how many of its offers wait on buyers (or one button, Turn on your agent), a notice with Set price while no usual price is given, then five rows, each changed in a panel on the same page: What you sell, Your price (usual and lowest), How you get paid (all at once, in stages or on delivery, and the days), What it does alone (make offers within the price, ask first, or agree inside the limits; set_up_my_agents changes it in a conversation) and When you buy (the most paid without asking and how long they can wait). More ways to get paid opens the full editor at /profile/ways for hourly, monthly and deposit ways. Where your record comes from has its own page, /profile/sources, linked from the Record card on Profile. A goods way also says whether its prices are for one item or the whole order, where they ship and how long it takes to arrive, a deposit way the deposit and the period. A way can carry a level under which the agent says no politely instead of asking (off unless set). The agent learns from the person’s own history and only suggests, never applies: a way to save after they said yes to a request of a kind they had not set up, a new usual price after three agreed deals, a no-ask level after three no answers; list_learned_suggestions lists them, propose_learned_change shows the How your agents deal card for one, dismiss_learned_suggestion remembers a no. The selling agent offers on a request inside the way of its kind, and for a request of a kind they do not offer it does not offer on its own: it tells them and they decide. Ways are shown under Your agents on Profile and changed at /profile/ways, or with set_way_i_deal, which shows a card and saves nothing until they confirm. A completed deal adds to your reputation, which ranks you in later matches. There is no guarantee of orders.",
    steps: ['Post an offer at /seller, for yourself or your business, or ask the assistant to draft one. The form is one screen: title, description, a category if you like, price and Ready in; Offer stays open, Lowest you accept and Pay in parts open in place, and it is one payment unless you open Pay in parts. Review shows the offer once more; Publish offer posts it, shows Publishing while it goes, then Your offer is live.', 'Add up to four photos on the form, or send them to the assistant before it drafts the offer.', "Add your skills on your profile so your seller agent makes offers on the right requests.", 'Share your offer link with people you already know.', "Review offers and matches at /seller; approve or decline what the agent brings."],
