    summary: 'A new deal first asks How do you want to pay? in two groups, showing only what runs: for work, One payment, In stages, A contest, and By the hour or week and Monthly where hourly work is on; for goods, Shipped and Handed over in person. A contest opens /contests/new and hourly work /work/new. Then one screen: the counterparty (Karwan tag, email or address) in one box, What will be delivered, the amount and the deadline; Pay in parts, how long they have to accept and a seller deposit open in place. Review shows the deal once more, and Send to the person sends the terms; nothing is paid then. Anyone, a person or a business, can sell goods: the form asks What it is (a service or goods) and, for goods, Shipped (a tracking number at delivery) or Handed over in person (the buyer\'s handover code); for a service, How you pay offers Fixed price or By the hour, which opens the hourly form with the person filled in. The kind of deal (one payment, stages or goods) is saved on the deal and the escrow uses it. Two deal rules are built and switched off on testnet: a seller with no finished deal and no verification takes up to 100 USDC, and goods over 50 USDC need shipped or in person. Creating the deal does not fund it. After seller agreement, the buyer reviews the current fee and exact total before funding. Selected identity or security-reserve requirements still apply. The assistant can build the whole deal from conversation, on the website and in chat: it asks only what is missing (what, how much, when), states the usual terms in one line, and shows one card with every term, goods terms included. Sending the deal moves no money. After the seller accepts, the payment card appears in the same conversation, and money moves only when the buyer confirms it. To trade again with someone from an earlier deal, the assistant lists the people you finished deals with (name, tag, what you traded, the amount) and builds the deal with them. Before any money is in the deal, the buyer can change it and the seller can counter (price, what is delivered, days to deliver), from the deal page or by asking the assistant (propose_change_deal_terms); the other side then agrees. The buyer can take back a deal the seller has not accepted, or one whose deadline passed with nothing delivered, and any money paid in comes back (propose_take_back_deal). In Telegram, taking a deal back opens the deal page, where it is confirmed. Only the buyer starts a protected deal; a seller who already agreed with someone sends them their deal link (share_my_deal_link, or Get paid by a client on Home), which opens this form with the seller filled in, and the seller then accepts. The link first asks how to pay with the person named under the title; every kind keeps them (by the hour or monthly opens the work form with them), and A contest is not offered because a contest is open to anyone.',
