    summary: 'On testnet, a person’s agents pay for their own market research from their own balance, through x402 on Arc settled by Circle Gateway: about 0.007 USDC per web search and 0.002 for one already run, sized to what is needed (an agent researching a request runs three: price, marketplace rates and demand). Each payment shows in what the agent spent. When an agent is short, it works on free data and the person is asked to add money to it. There is no research credit to buy any more; credit left from before is being returned to people. A record check costs 0.005 USDC: a selling agent checks the buyer once before offering on a request (0.005 USDC), a buying agent checks up to five sellers on its shortlist (at most 0.025 USDC per request), and no more are paid on one request. Checks are paid from the agent data balance, the person’s own USDC prepaid on Circle Gateway; when it runs low the agent moves 0.10 USDC into it from its own wallet, which the activity shows as moved to the agent data balance, not as money spent. get_my_agent gives the price, the cost per request and what is left. Each person’s agents have a weekly budget for the data they pay for, 0.25 USDC unless the person changes it (set_agent_budget, 0 to 5 USDC; 0 means free data only). An agent never goes over it: a paid check or search that would is not made, the agent carries on with free data, and the person hears once a week that the budget was reached. A search the person asks for says when it would go over and offers to raise the budget. Once a week, on by default, the person gets one line in the app and on Telegram on what their agents spent and what for (set_weekly_report turns it off). get_my_agent shows the budget, what was spent in the last 7 days, the weekly line and the market watches. A person’s agent also says what it sees about how they trade, from Karwan’s own deals only and never from a model: a request budget far from what deals of that kind settled at (on the test network, a budget above that range, with the middle price to use), requests the seller missed because their lowest price sat above what buyers offered, cheaper sellers with as good a record on a request they are about to accept, and a request with no offer after a day that allows fewer days than sellers asked for on similar ones. At most three, the biggest change first, and the same one not twice in a week unless its number moved. They come in the weekly line and whenever the person asks (whats_my_agent_seeing). Each comes with one step the person confirms: a request budget or due date is fixed on chain, so changing it means taking the request down and posting it again. To research something yourself, ask the assistant (research_market), which says the cost first. Not open on mainnet, where agents will pay Circle marketplace services directly.',
