    id: 'outside-agents', title: 'Deals from agents outside Karwan', status: 'testnet', mainnet: 'off', route: '/agent-jobs',
    pages: ['/agent-jobs', '/agent-jobs/[ref]', '/agent-jobs/release/[token]', '/pair/[token]', '/settings'],
    api: ['GET /api/agent-jobs/mine', 'GET /api/agent-jobs/:ref', 'POST /api/agent-jobs/:ref/delivered', 'POST /api/agent-jobs/:ref/dispute', 'GET /api/agent-jobs/pair/:token', 'POST /api/agent-jobs/pair/:token', 'GET /api/agent-jobs/release/:token', 'POST /api/agent-jobs/release/:token/check', 'POST /api/agent-jobs/release/:token'],
    tools: [],
    keywords: 'outside agent mcp claude chatgpt bot agentkit pair pairing release link verified person deal funded by an agent accept deals from agents outside karwan',
    summary: 'Agents outside Karwan, such as Claude, ChatGPT or a company\'s own bot, can work for one person through the Karwan MCP server at https://api.karwan.site/mcp, on Arc Testnet only. Every request carries a World AgentKit proof that one real person is behind the agent. The agent finds sellers who fit a need (find_counterparty, 0.10 USDC) and checks a member\'s public record (check_person, 0.005 USDC), both paid with x402 from a Circle Gateway balance; a refused call is never charged. Karwan matches inside on full records and answers with tag, tier, reasons, rating, price and days, never a score or counts. To open a deal (open_protected_deal) the person behind the agent first verifies once with World ID on a Karwan link the agent sends them, /pair/<link>; they need no Karwan account. The agent then gets the quote, the work plus half the 1 percent fee, and the exact calls to send from its own wallet: create the job, then (fund_deal) set the budget, approve and fund. Karwan reads each one back from Arc. The seller sees the deal in Deals from outside agents (/agent-jobs) as funded by an agent for a verified person, and marks it delivered with a note on its page. The agent asks for a one-time link (request_release, or open_dispute when the person is not happy) and sends it to its person, who answers on Karwan with the same World ID: happy pays the seller, not happy sends the seller their one line and gives them 3 days to dispute, otherwise the money goes back to the agent\'s wallet. The agent cannot answer the link and cannot pay the seller. If the person says nothing for the 5 days of review, the seller is paid, and a day before that the agent is told to remind its person. A seller who misses the deadline is not paid and the agent gets the refund call. Sellers take these deals unless they turn off Accept deals from agents outside Karwan in Settings. There are no extra caps on a verified person; one deal can be up to about 1,000 USDC of work on testnet. Posting a request through an outside agent is not available yet.',
    steps: ['The outside agent connects to the Karwan MCP server and finds a seller who fits.', 'The person behind it verifies once with World ID on the link the agent sends.', 'The agent opens and funds the deal from its own wallet; the seller is told and delivers, then marks it delivered on its page.', 'The person answers the release link: happy pays the seller, not happy gives the seller 3 days to dispute.'],
    sources: ['backend/src/agentJobs/agentJobs.ts', 'backend/src/mcp/server.ts', 'docs/architecture/15-outside-agents.md'],
