    keywords: 'silent stuck seller buyer reclaim refund dispute cancellation deadline release recovery legacy old contract previous escrow before new reconcile',
    summary: 'Recovery depends on whether funding, delivery, a release or a dispute has occurred and on the deployed contract and current timers. Read the specific deal and open its Next step view. If the parties cannot agree a split, each side tells Karwan its side within 72 hours by answering three questions on the deal page (Tell Karwan your side, Answer by the date). Karwan checks both sides, the delivery and the deal chat, proposes a split, and a person on the Karwan team confirms it before any money moves; nothing in the check moves money itself. Say it that way: Karwan is checking, never a judge or a reviewer. The panel also says Karwan support will never message you outside Karwan or ask you to send money; repeat that when someone says a person contacted them about a dispute. A side that does not answer in time loses. An open problem shows its steps at the top of the deal page: who opened it, when the other side answers by (or The answer date passed. Karwan is checking), and Karwan decides, with the line that the money is held by Karwan until it is decided. While the seller has not answered, the buyer reads that if the seller does not answer by the date, Karwan returns the money to the buyer after a check: the silent-seller rule proposes it and a reviewer confirms it first, so never say it happens on its own. Do not promise an immediate refund, a universal grace period, or recovery without the seller in every disputed state. Never advise paying again or releasing money to unlock a refund. Money still on an older Karwan contract is listed and returned at /legacy (Profile, Other, Earlier deals), for as long as the contract holds it. Once the new escrow is live on a network (on testnet since 24 Oct 2026), every deal that opened before it is listed at /legacy under Deals from before the new escrow, open ones first, so people can reconcile them; its deal page says it finishes in Earlier deals and links there, with no moves of its own, and list_my_deals marks them previousEscrow. Market, Your trades links to the list when there are any. A missed delivery date refunds the buyer automatically once the grace period after it ends, unless the seller\'s request for more time is still waiting on the buyer: that holds the refund until the buyer answers. The buyer has the review time the deal set, at most 30 days, to check each delivery. They can release, ask once for more time (propose_more_review_time), or raise a problem with what is wrong (propose_raise_problem). A day before review ends Karwan reminds them. When review ends with no release and no problem raised, the payment goes to the seller; on deals held by the new escrow Karwan pays it then. A buyer cannot raise a problem after their review time ends.',
