    summary: 'Profile shows your record in one line, Your record with your level and deals completed (or New on Karwan before the first deal), and it opens your Trade record page at /credit-passport/<address>. That page holds every line: your standing and score, Deals (settled, completed and disputes in one card, then volume, different people traded with, the deal guarantee in place, the last deal, How this is worked out and Proof on Arc), More (What others see, Earlier deals and Where your record comes from) and Share full record as its main button; only the owner sees those counts. Under it one Money row shows the same one figure as Money and opens it (the balance, the agent and the deal guarantee all live there). Then Trading (Buying with open requests, Selling with live offers, Your agent with its status, and the assistant switch), Account (Contact, Wallets, Business profile, Passkey, Account recovery), Preferences (Language, Theme, Show amounts in, More settings), Help and how it works, and Sign out with Terms and Privacy under it; Edit profile is the button beside the name, and the workspace switcher shows only when there is a business workspace. What others see is the public record at /r/<tag>: the photo, the name, the tag and country, three facts in one card (deals done, the average rating and the share on time; before a first deal, the average rating, how many rated them and the tier name), up to three reasons, what the person sells as rows with a photo and price, their recent deals (date, side and value range, each with its signed statement to check), and one button to ask them for an offer, never the score, an exact amount or who the deals were with. After a deal settles, both people are asked to rate each other from 1 to 5 with an optional note, within 3 days of settling; the ask links straight to the rating on the deal page (rate_deal; my_ratings_to_give lists what is waiting). A rating shows as soon as it is given, with one reminder after 3 days for anyone who has not rated. Each person’s public rating is the mean with its count, for example 4.8 from 23 deals; under 3 ratings it shows New. Ratings from disputed deals are counted beside the number, for example 3.7 from 3 deals, 2 disputed, and rating closes 14 days after the deal settles. A note with a phone number, an email or a link is kept private. The rating is separate from the reputation score, which it does not change. Reputation reflects completed Karwan deals and has completion and concentration limits. Posting a request or an offer lets the agents of people on that request check your record with a paid, logged read; agents outside Karwan can only if you allow it in Profile. An agent pays for a person’s record once per request: checking it again on the same request uses the same read unless their record changed, and each payment shows in what the agent spent. Other people see your tier, reasons and deal counts, never your score or your amounts, unless you share your full passport: from your own passport (Share full record) or by asking the assistant on any channel (share_my_passport), you open it to one person by Karwan tag, who must be signed in as that person, or to anyone holding the link, for 24 hours or 7 days. They then see what you see, amounts and the money held as a reserve included. At most five shares are live at once; each shows who it is for, until when and how often it was opened, and you can stop any of them at any time (my_passport_shares, stop_passport_share), after which the link shows the sealed passport again. Each deal that settles from the day it was switched on leaves a signed, attested statement for each side (role, date, amount range, never the other person); earlier deals only on request. Turn it off or use Remove my published deals in Settings. Declared skills are not verified skills. A deal guarantee is money a person sets aside to protect their buyers and back advances from financiers (propose_guarantee_put_up). It counts toward the reputation score. Deals and advances can hold part of it until they finish. Withdrawing it (propose_guarantee_take_out) brings it back after 7 days; withdrawing more restarts the 7 days for everything coming back. While it comes back it no longer protects deals. The wait can be cancelled (propose_guarantee_cancel_take_out), and the money is collected once it is ready (propose_guarantee_collect); get_my_guarantee shows what is in place, held, coming back and ready. A guarantee earns at the USYC rate, paid by Karwan on testnet and claimed on /guarantee (propose_claim_yield); never say the guarantee itself is invested in USYC, and yield is never promised. Guarantees deposited before stay on the previous contract: the guarantee page shows the amount with a link to withdraw it from Earlier deals. Earlier deals (/legacy, from More on the Trade record page) lists everything a person still has on older Karwan contracts, older deals and older guarantees, each with the one step that works now; get_my_legacy_positions and propose_legacy_step do the same from chat. A row Karwan cannot return by itself says so and is returned by support. A wallet account signs each step in its own wallet; in Telegram that step is done in the Karwan app. Reputation is not proof of identity or honesty. Someone with their own wallet can also deposit to their deal guarantee from the assistant: the card opens their wallet to sign it, together with any steps their record still needs.',
    steps: ['Tap Your record on /profile to open your Trade record page; what others see is at /r/[tag] (Trade record, More, What others see).', 'To show someone your full record, tap Share full record on that page, or ask the assistant: pick One person by tag or Anyone with the link, and 24 hours or 7 days, then Create link; Copy link is the main button once it is made, and Done closes it.', 'Each settled deal Karwan attested opens as a readable statement at /attested/[id], with the signed credential one link further for machines.', 'The deal guarantee is the third part of Money (/account?tab=guarantee; /guarantee lands there): the amount in place is the largest line with an info tip on what it does, then Add and Withdraw, then Earns, Holding for deals, Ready to withdraw and Coming back with its date, and Earnings on your guarantee folds under one row. It shows no score. Add, withdraw, collect or keep it in each open their own page, or ask the assistant.', 'Money on older contracts: Trade record, More, Earlier deals, at /legacy.'],
